Unexpected DevOps Issue I Faced 🚨
Everything was working fine until a new node joined the Kubernetes cluster 🖥️

 Suddenly, a few pods started failing randomly ❌

🔍 Root Cause:

Nodes had different time zones / clock drift ⏱️
Application tokens were time-sensitive
Requests were getting rejected due to time mismatch

🛠️ How it was fixed:

 ✅ Synced time using NTP (chrony) on all nodes
 ✅ Restarted affected pods
 ✅ Verified time consistency across the cluster

📌 Lesson learned:

 In distributed systems, even time can break your application.
 Consistency matters more than we think ⏳
